<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jovan Nenad</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1527</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Tsar Jovan Nenad</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jovan Nenad was a Serbian leader who, after the Ottoman victory at Mohács in 1526, gathered an army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbs">Serbs</a> in the southern Hungarian plain and proclaimed himself tsar, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/subotica">Subotica</a> over much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/backa">Bačka</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banat">Banat</a>. In the contest for the Hungarian throne he turned from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-zapolya">John Zápolya</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-i-holy-roman-emperor">Ferdinand of Habsburg</a>, and he was defeated and killed by Zápolya's forces in 1527.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jovan-nenad.jpg" alt="Jovan Nenad" width="217" height="311" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: sr:user:Саша.Стефановић · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tsar_Jovan_Nenad_monument_crop.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
